$CATEGORY: Q1 - COMPILING A PROGRAMM

::Q101:: 
High-level language is designed to be easy for humans to read and write. {TRUE}

::Q102:: 
Low-level language is designed to be easy for a computer to run.  {TRUE}

::Q103:: Examples of high-level languages {
    ~%50%Python
    ~%50%C++
    ~%-100%Machine language
}

::Q104:: Low-level programs are portable {FALSE}

::Q105:: 
To interpret is{
    =To run a high-level program by translating it one line at a time and immediately executing the corresponding instructions.
    ~To translate a program in a high-level language into a low-level language, all at once, in preparation for later execution.
}

::Q106:: 
To compile is{
    ~To run a high-level program by translating it one line at a time and immediately executing the corresponding instructions.
    =To translate a program in a high-level language into a low-level language, all at once, in preparation for later execution.
}

::Q107:: 
Source code{
    =A program in a high-level language, before being compiled.
    ~The output of the compiler, after translating the program.
}

::Q108::
Object code{
    ~A program in a high-level language, before being compiled.
    =The output of the compiler, after translating the program.
}

::Q109::
An executable is another name for object code that is ready to run on specific hardware. {TRUE}

$CATEGORY:Q2 - COMPUTER SCIENCE

::Q201::
An algorithm is a procedure or formula for solving a problem, with or without a computer.{
    TRUE}

::Q202::
Computer science is the scientific and practical approach to computation and its applications. {TRUE}

::Q203::
A program is a sequence of instructions that specifies how to perform tasks on a computer. {TRUE}

::Q203::
Basic instructions in a program are {
    ~%25%input and output
    ~%25%math
    ~%25%decision
    ~%25%repetition (loops)
    ~%-100%finding the roots of a polynomial
}

::Q204::
The application of problem solving to creating executable computer programs is also known as {
    =programming
    ~compiling
    ~computer science
}

$CATEGORY: Q3 - JAVA

::Q301::
The meaninng of JVM and JDK is {
    =Java Virtual Machine and Java Development Kit
    ~Java Virtual Machine and Java Development Key
    ~Java Virtual Machine and Java Design Kit
}

::Q302::
The JVM enables a computer to run Java programs.{TRUE}

::Q303::
A byte code is similar to object code, but it is portable like a high-level language.{TRUE}
